cicada audition <score.cicada> [flags]

report what a score sounds like

Flags:
  -o <directory>             write spectrogram.png, chroma.png, rhythm.png and energy.png, and bar-range pages of the spectrogram and chroma when the range is wider than --image-width
  --from <bar>               one-based start bar (default 1)
  --bars <n>                 bars to analyze; 0 means through song end
  --tracks <a,b>             analyze only these tracks and the mix; an unknown name fails with the valid names
  --peaks <n>                true-peak moments of the mix to list, 0 to 100 (default 10; 0 lists none)
  --bar-bands                add each track's level in each band per bar (tracks[].bar_bands_db; seven numbers per track per bar)
  --no-bands                 skip band ownership, which takes about an eighth of the CPU time
  --image-width <px>         widest picture in pixels (default 1600; 0 keeps one full-resolution strip)
  --json                     write the report as JSON (format cicada.audition/1)
  --max-resident-pcm <size>  cap on decoded sampler-pack PCM held in memory, such as 2GiB (default 1GiB)
  --cpuprofile <file>        write a Go CPU profile of the command to file
  --help                     show this help

Renders the mix and stems, then reports heard key, written and heard chords per bar, per-track level, brightness, attack, decay and rhythm, the mix's loudness per bar, beat and section (BS.1770), which track owns each of seven frequency bands per bar and where two collide, which tracks sound in each bar, repeated bars, silences, and the highest true peaks with the tracks that set them. See docs/manual/audition.md. CICADA_MAX_RESIDENT_PCM sets the sampler-pack cap when the option is omitted.
